From: Eric Tanner <eric.tanner@harvia.com>
Subject: [PATCH] am62lx: env: default optargs, hide the fbcon cursor

args_mmc (include/env/ti/mmc.env) expands ${optargs} into bootargs, but
nothing gives optargs a value and this board's bootcmd does not load
uEnv.txt, so the kernel has always booted with none. The display now
comes up inside the kernel and fbcon draws the boot logo on the panel:

  vt.global_cursor_default=0   no text cursor blinking over the logo
                               and over psplash
  fbcon=logo-pos:center        centre the logo (where psplash draws the
                               same artwork), not top-left
  fbcon=logo-count:1           one logo, not one per online CPU

Signed-off-by: Eric Tanner <eric.tanner@harvia.com>
  cpufreq.default_governor=ondemand
                               the kernel's defconfig default is
                               "performance"; with the A53 OPP table from
                               recipes-kernel/linux (cpufreq through the
                               SCMI clock) ondemand keeps the boot at the
                               top OPP under load and lets the idle app
                               sit at 600 MHz.
---
--- a/board/ti/am62lx/am62lx.env
+++ b/board/ti/am62lx/am62lx.env
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 
 name_kern=Image
 console=ttyS0,115200n8
+optargs=vt.global_cursor_default=0 fbcon=logo-pos:center,logo-count:1 cpufreq.default_governor=ondemand
 args_all=setenv optargs ${optargs} earlycon=ns16550a,mmio32,0x02800000
 	${mtdparts}
 run_kern=booti ${loadaddr} ${rd_spec} ${fdtaddr}
